# Combine Documents and Change Orders into One App

## Summary

Use **haysfwco as the main app**, bringing in the full document generator from **haysdocuments-2**.

Each saved job will have **Job Details, Documents, and Change Requests**. Documents can be generated before a change request exists. Shared details are entered once and reused throughout the workflow.

## User experience

- Keep the current review dashboard and Quick Request flow; add **Jobs & Documents** to navigation.
- Open a job to edit customer, property, insurance, financial, mortgage, team, and production details.
- Provide all current document types, editable previews, individual downloads, combined packets, ZIP downloads, estimate intake, and AI-assisted filling.
- Start change requests from a job with its details prefilled. Show related requests and generated documents together.
- Keep the existing customer change-order editor as the single preparation workflow. Its Documents entry opens the appropriate request.
- Combined packets may include a selected change order; jobs without one generate their other documents normally.

## Implementation

- **Shared job records:** Add permanent job workspace IDs independent of CSV directory IDs. Add an optional workspace reference to change requests while preserving their existing snapshots and estimator corrections.
- **Safe storage:** Extend the current change-order Apps Script backend with separate workspace and document storage. CSV replacements must never erase saved job details, requests, or documents.
- **Document integration:** Move the generator’s templates, field editing, intake parser, and readiness checks into a lazily loaded module. Adapt its styling and remove global PDF-library patches that could affect the existing change-order generator.
- **Cloud services:** Store generated PDFs through Apps Script and Drive. Run DeepSeek through Apps Script Properties, keeping its key server-side. Keep directory imports and customer reference imports separate.
- **Saving:** Retain durable local autosave for document work, with background synchronization and visible pending/error states. Use revision checks and stable retry IDs to prevent lost edits or duplicate files.
- **Financial accuracy:** Keep approved RCV and original contract amounts distinct. Preserve exact cents, credits, explicit zero, and unknown prices. Estimators remain responsible for final change-order prices.
- **Existing data:** Provide a repeatable export/import migration for saved generator jobs and device drafts. Match only unique job numbers automatically; present ambiguous matches for selection. Preserve original records and existing Drive files.

New backend actions cover listing/opening/saving workspaces, saving/fetching job documents, and intake analysis; existing request APIs remain compatible.

## Verification and rollout

- Verify shared details populate new requests without overwriting existing request corrections.
- Test CSV replacement, migration retries, duplicate job numbers, offline recovery, competing edits, failed uploads, and lost responses.
- Check every PDF type, editable previews, long text, checklist boxes, packet assembly, and financial calculations.
- Run unit, backend, build, and browser checks; verify the installed mobile PWA before release.
- Deploy the compatible Apps Script backend first, then test a frontend preview before updating the main app.

Current local baseline: both apps pass TypeScript checks, and all **44 change-order unit tests pass**.

## Defaults

- Google Apps Script, Sheets, and Drive remain the backend.
- Keep the current app entry flow and installed PWA identity.
- The existing document app stays available during migration.
- Windows Electron packaging is outside this integration.
